{
  "info": {
    "_postman_id": "5219303f-a6e2-46ef-9630-06b0ed844f0b",
    "name": "equis-my-riders",
    "description": "Riding Schedule \u2014 E5 my riders and level changes (M5) against equis-api: GET /me/riders, GET /me/riders/{id}/level-history and POST /me/riders/{id}/level-change.\n\nBefore running:\n1. Dev database with V1\u2013V14 applied and sessions generated: trainer 1 is active and has at least one rider on levels 1\u20135 (the V12 seed gives three on Level 1).\n2. trainerLogin / trainerPassword default to seeded trainer 1.\n\nRun order: 0 \u2192 3. Folder 1 picks the rider (one with a next session if there is one), folder 2 remembers their seats and history, folder 3 promotes them and demotes them back.\nSide effects that stay: the rider's upcoming seats in their starting level are freed, and each run adds two history lines.\nSkipped when the data is not there: level_at_top / level_at_bottom (no rider of mine on Level 6 / Level 1) and the 422 seat check (the rider had no upcoming seat).\nNot covered here: another trainer's rider (answered like an unknown id, 404 rider_not_found) and the admin token (403 forbidden).",
    "schema": "https://schema.getpostman.com/json/collection/v2.1.0/collection.json"
  },
  "item": [
    {
      "name": "0 \u00b7 Sign in",
      "description": "Run first: every other request uses trainerAccessToken.",
      "item": [
        {
          "name": "Trainer login \u2192 200",
          "request": {
            "method": "POST",
            "header": [
              {
                "key": "Content-Type",
                "value": "application/json"
              }
            ],
            "url": {
              "raw": "{{baseUrl}}/auth/login",
              "host": [
                "{{baseUrl}}"
              ],
              "path": [
                "auth",
                "login"
              ]
            },
            "description": "Saves trainerAccessToken (valid for 15 minutes).",
            "body": {
              "mode": "raw",
              "raw": "{\n  \"login\": \"{{trainerLogin}}\",\n  \"password\": \"{{trainerPassword}}\",\n  \"rememberMe\": false\n}",
              "options": {
                "raw": {
                  "language": "json"
                }
              }
            }
          },
          "event": [
            {
              "listen": "test",
              "script": {
                "type": "text/javascript",
                "exec": [
                  "pm.test(\"Status 200\", () => pm.response.to.have.status(200));",
                  "const b = pm.response.json();",
                  "pm.test(\"role = TRAINER\", () => pm.expect(b.role).to.eql(\"TRAINER\"));",
                  "pm.collectionVariables.set(\"trainerAccessToken\", b.accessToken);"
                ]
              }
            }
          ]
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "name": "1 \u00b7 My riders (M5)",
      "description": "GET /me/riders answers the whole list; tabs, counts and search are done in the app. The first request picks the rider the rest of the collection moves.",
      "item": [
        {
          "name": "All my riders \u2192 200",
          "request": {
            "method": "GET",
            "header": [
              {
                "key": "Authorization",
                "value": "Bearer {{trainerAccessToken}}"
              }
            ],
            "url": {
              "raw": "{{baseUrl}}/me/riders",
              "host": [
                "{{baseUrl}}"
              ],
              "path": [
                "me",
                "riders"
              ]
            }
          },
          "event": [
            {
              "listen": "test",
              "script": {
                "type": "text/javascript",
                "exec": [
                  "pm.test(\"Status 200\", () => pm.response.to.have.status(200));",
                  "const b = pm.response.json();",
                  "pm.test(\"Is an array\", () => pm.expect(b).to.be.an(\"array\"));",
                  "pm.test(\"Each rider has the contract fields\", () => b.forEach(r => {",
                  "    pm.expect(r.id).to.match(/^[0-9a-f-]{36}$/);",
                  "    pm.expect(r.name).to.be.a(\"string\");",
                  "    pm.expect(r.initials).to.be.a(\"string\");",
                  "    pm.expect(r.levelId).to.be.within(1, 6);",
                  "    pm.expect(r.since).to.match(/^\\d{4}-\\d{2}-\\d{2}$/);",
                  "    pm.expect(r).to.have.property(\"nextSession\");",
                  "    pm.expect(r).to.not.have.property(\"phone\");",
                  "    if (r.nextSession) { pm.expect(r.nextSession.date).to.match(/^\\d{4}-\\d{2}-\\d{2}$/); pm.expect(r.nextSession.start).to.match(/^\\d{2}:\\d{2}$/); pm.expect(r.nextSession.end).to.match(/^\\d{2}:\\d{2}$/); }",
                  "}));",
                  "// The rider is promoted and then demoted back, so any level below 6 works; prefer one with a next session so the freed seats show.",
                  "const movable = b.filter(r => r.levelId <= 5);",
                  "const pick = movable.find(r => r.nextSession) || movable[0];",
                  "pm.test(\"Has a rider on levels 1\u20135 to move\", () => pm.expect(pick).to.exist);",
                  "pm.collectionVariables.set(\"riderId\", pick.id);",
                  "pm.collectionVariables.set(\"riderName\", pick.name);",
                  "pm.collectionVariables.set(\"riderLevel\", String(pick.levelId));",
                  "pm.collectionVariables.set(\"riderLevelUp\", String(pick.levelId + 1));",
                  "// Riders already at the ends, if I have any, for level_at_top / level_at_bottom.",
                  "const top = b.find(r => r.levelId === 6), bottom = b.find(r => r.levelId === 1);",
                  "pm.collectionVariables.set(\"topRiderId\", top ? top.id : \"\");",
                  "pm.collectionVariables.set(\"bottomRiderId\", bottom ? bottom.id : \"\");"
                ]
              }
            }
          ]
        },
